WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.000
Speaker 1: Hey, David, is there anyone who
would run against Trump in the Republican

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.470
primary instead of letting him have the nomination
if he wants it?

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:10.510
This is a great question.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:17.189
The context is that last week, former ambassador
to the U.N. Nikki Haley said even though at

00:00:17.189 --> 00:00:22.930
one point a couple of months ago she was kind
of critical of Trump, she said, if Trump runs,

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:25.680
I wouldn't run in twenty, twenty four.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:28.519
And if Trump runs, I would support Donald
Trump.

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:33.020
I think most of the people right now that
are contenders for the Republican primary

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:36.109
in 2024 would get the hell out of the way
and let Trump have it.

00:00:36.109 --> 00:00:39.859
It just took Mike Pompeo, Trump's secretary
of state, as mentioned.

00:00:39.859 --> 00:00:43.359
I don't even think Pompeo is a candidate,
but there's no there's no chance in hell that

00:00:43.359 --> 00:00:45.000
Pompeo runs against Donald Trump.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:49.340
If I was thinking about it and Trump runs
Pompeo out of the way, I don't think Mike

00:00:49.340 --> 00:00:50.520
Pence would run against Donald Trump.

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:52.510
That would be really weird.

00:00:52.510 --> 00:00:55.800
Former vice president running against the
person they served under.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.800
Don't think it's going to happen.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:02.089
Ron, to this is being mentioned, the Republican
Florida governor, who is horrible in every

00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:05.630
way he would not run against Donald Trump.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:13.240
Um, Josh Hawley, who was one of the first
defiantly and and proudly opposing the certification

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:14.670
of the twenty twenty election results.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:19.860
He's not running against Trump, Ted Cruz not
running against Trump.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:23.360
Kristi Noem, the South Carolina governor,
she's a Trump suck up.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.440
She's not going to run against them.

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.409
Lindsey Graham, forget about it.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:29.150
A Rick Scott.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:37.090
I don't see any of these people actually challenging
Trump unless something dramatic were to happen

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:40.549
around the twenty, twenty two midterms.

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:44.820
I think that the people who would stay in
if Trump runs.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:50.060
Are the people who would be running because
they don't like Trump, people like Mitt Romney,

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:51.060
who else?

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.560
I don't even know.

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:53.960
I can't even think of anybody else.

00:01:53.960 --> 00:01:59.689
Mitt Romney types are the ones that wouldn't
get out of the way for Trump because they

00:01:59.689 --> 00:02:02.320
are not Trump's fundamentally.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:10.940
And I think that Trump's 20 24 future will
be far more determined by Trump's physical

00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:19.769
health at the time and whether Trump's urge
for revenge and pettiness override laziness.

00:02:19.769 --> 00:02:27.099
And I think that Trump spending four years
at Mar a Lago, the idea of of I mean, you

00:02:27.099 --> 00:02:32.040
know, the campaign fuels his narcissism, the
crowds and the speeches and the media coverage.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.820
There's no doubt about it.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:37.690
But at the same time, he's not a particularly
healthy guy.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.520
He'll be close to 80 at that time.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.550
I think he will be relatively bored and complacent.

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:50.500
And it will really be Trump who determines
what happens in 2024 as of right now, if it

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:54.590
if it's Trump versus Romney today, I think
Trump certainly wins.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:59.570
Trump has the support of the vast majority
of the Republican Party, but don't expect

00:02:59.570 --> 00:03:05.519
the challenge to Trump by anyone from within
the Trump circle.

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:09.580
Could could Liz Cheney maybe challenge Trump?

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:12.120
Yeah, maybe somebody like that.

00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.239
Condoleezza Rice?

00:03:14.239 --> 00:03:15.239
I don't know.

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:18.590
I'm thinking out loud, but most of the people
that have been around Trump are not going

00:03:18.590 --> 00:04:05.459
to challenge Donald Trump if Donald Trump
decides 

00:04:05.459 --> 00:04:56.370
to run.

